{
  // Announcements that send themselves, with no staff member having to press anything.
  //
  // Everything below is commented out on purpose, so a fresh server announces nothing at all. Take the
  // // off the lines of an example to switch it on, or write your own.
  //
  // Each announcement takes:
  //   name          a short label so you can find it again in the menu. Never shown to players.
  //   text          what everybody actually sees. Written exactly as you type it, never translated.
  //   everyMinutes  send it this often, counting from when the server started. Between 1 and 1440.
  //   at            send it at this time of day instead, written as HH:MM on a 24 hour clock.
  //   clock         which clock this announcement measures itself against. It applies to "everyMinutes"
  //                 and to "at" alike. "real" is the real world, so 30 minutes is half an hour and 20:00
  //                 is eight in the evening where your server runs. "game" is the clock inside GTA, which
  //                 runs much faster, so 30 game minutes come round in about a real minute and 20:00 lands
  //                 whenever it turns evening in the world. Leave it out and you get "real".
  //
  // Use either "everyMinutes" or "at" on one announcement, never both. An announcement with neither is
  // skipped and says so in the server console.
  //
  // An "at" announcement that the server started past waits for the next time round rather than firing
  // the moment it loads, so restarting at 20:05 will not replay your 20:00 message.
  //
  // Staff with the ManageAnnouncements permission can also add and remove announcements from inside the
  // menu, which rewrites this file. Comments you leave in here are not kept when that happens.
  //
  // The whole thing can also be switched off without deleting anything, by setting
  // vMenu.Enhanced.Admin.ScheduledAnnouncements to false in your configuration.cfg.
  //
  // Deleting this file is fine. It just means nothing announces itself.

  "announcements": [
